{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "units": [
    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher",
      "title": "Actual standardized RGO position and Fisher",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex8",
          "label": "SPHMC Ex8/p4.2/p4.3 and scoped4.6; affine prerequisite",
          "scope": "Source realκ>=1,beta1/alphakappainv,C2/globalbothcurvature and every0<eta<=1 retained. Fullfinite real Hilbert/Borel incl0 and arbitrary measurableS are disclosed extensions. Actualp,normalizedmu/R/r,affinelaw,curvature/stationarity andtrue moments are all outputs, never certificates. Generic canonical affine transport needs only nonzero scale and proves identity of Mathlib normalized tilts; it does not assert a probability law without produced positive integrability. GaussianTalagrand/LSI/FIRSTW2 inequality4.6,bias4.2/MGF4.3/fullLemma4.2,higher/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization,posteriorjointMarkovsemantics,actualsamplers/PBPSreflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation,main/work/composition OPEN. Actualr/R distinct from Gaussiangradientoutput and HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Numericalprox sourcecapeta<=1/(2beta) remains; TV never transfers unboundedcost."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Source beta=1, alpha=kappa^-1, real kappa>=1; actual C2 V with kappa^-1*normv^2<=D2V(x)[v,v]<=normv^2 for every x,v.",
        "Finite real complete Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero, and arbitrary measurable parameter space S; measurable eta/y with every0<eta(s)<=1. These coordinate-free and parameter-space extensions are disclosed.",
        "No supplied proximal point, law identity, normalizer, probability, curvature, gradient or moment certificate. Actual p, mu/R/r probability, normalized affine law, C2 curvature/mode and genuine position/Fisher L2 are internally produced. The numerical-prox eta<=1/(2beta) cap is a separate computational contract."
      ],
      "statement": "Produce one measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. For literal rho(u)=V(p+sqrteta*u)-V(p)-sqrteta*inner(gradientV(p),u) and Q=normu^2/2+rho, produce C2, mode0, 0<=Hessrho<=etaI and I<=HessQ<=(1+eta)I. The actual RGO R=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)) is a probability measure, and its actual standardized pushforward r equals volume.tilted(-Q). Genuine position and rho-gradient L2 satisfy integral normu^2 dr<=d and integral normgradrho^2 dr<=eta^2 integral normu^2 dr<=eta^2 d. Only the last TWO comparisons of(4.6) are covered; the first W2 comparison is open.",
      "formula": "r=(x\\mapsto (x-p)/\\sqrt\\eta)_\\#R=Z_Q^{-1}e^{-Q(u)}du,\\quad\\int\\|\\nabla\\rho\\|^2dr\\le\\eta^2\\int\\|u\\|^2dr\\le\\eta^2d.",
      "boundary": "Source realκ>=1,beta1/alphakappainv,C2/globalbothcurvature and every0<eta<=1 retained. Fullfinite real Hilbert/Borel incl0 and arbitrary measurableS are disclosed extensions. Actualp,normalizedmu/R/r,affinelaw,curvature/stationarity andtrue moments are all outputs, never certificates. Generic canonical affine transport needs only nonzero scale and proves identity of Mathlib normalized tilts; it does not assert a probability law without produced positive integrability. GaussianTalagrand/LSI/FIRSTW2 inequality4.6,bias4.2/MGF4.3/fullLemma4.2,higher/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization,posteriorjointMarkovsemantics,actualsamplers/PBPSreflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation,main/work/composition OPEN. Actualr/R distinct from Gaussiangradientoutput and HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Numericalprox sourcecapeta<=1/(2beta) remains; TV never transfers unboundedcost.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Produce the true proximal point and base law",
          "text": "Positive source curvature yields exp(-V) integrability and a probability mu. Reuse the actual full-range measurable proximal producer, preserving p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. There is no selector or probability premise.",
          "formula": "\\mu=Z_V^{-1}e^{-V}dx,\\quad p_s+\\eta_s\\nabla V(p_s)=y_s.",
          "lean": "StrongConvexGibbsIntegrability.integrable_exp_neg_of_strongConvexOn; HessianStrongConvexity; FullRangeProximalGaussianOracle"
        },
        {
          "title": "Differentiate the literal standardized potential",
          "text": "Apply genuine affine chain rules and the real Hilbert Riesz gradient to the literal rho and Q. The linear term cancels the gradient at zero; the quadratic term contributes the identity Hessian.",
          "formula": "\\nabla\\rho(u)=\\sqrt\\eta[\\nabla V(p+\\sqrt\\eta u)-\\nabla V(p)],\\quad D^2\\rho=\\eta D^2V,\\quad D^2Q=I+\\eta D^2V.",
          "lean": "actual_standardized_calculus; HasFDerivAt.comp; inner_gradient_left; HasFDerivAt.norm_sq"
        },
        {
          "title": "Derive actual curvature and the mode",
          "text": "Retained source curvature and positive eta give 0<=Hessrho<=etaI and I<=HessQ<=(1+eta)I, with both real gradients zero at zero. C2 is produced from V; none of these estimates is supplied.",
          "formula": "\\nabla\\rho(0)=\\nabla Q(0)=0,\\quad 0\\preceq D^2\\rho\\preceq\\eta I,\\quad I\\preceq D^2Q\\preceq(1+\\eta)I.",
          "lean": "actual_standardized_calculus; hH; mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left"
        },
        {
          "title": "Produce genuine Q normalization and the position moment",
          "text": "Apply the accepted noncompact Gibbs position-moment producer to the actual Q with alpha1,beta1+eta and mode0. Its actual weighted IBP proves the required ordinary-volume L1 product integrability and applies full-space Fubini/IBP, without a cutoff assumption or construction, yielding positive partition, probability and positionL2. The current source theorem assumes no IBP or moment certificate.",
          "formula": "\\int\\langle u,\\nabla Q(u)\\rangle dr=d,\\quad\\int\\|u\\|^2dr\\le d.",
          "lean": "GibbsPositionMoment.gibbs_position_moment; memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm"
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the literal true RGO law",
          "text": "Combine the actual two tilts into W=V+norm(x-y)^2/(2eta). Exact proximal optimality gives W(p+sqrteta*u)=Q(u)+C, with C=V(p)+norm(p-y)^2/(2eta). Apply canonical affine transport, then cancel C using the internally produced Q probability and integrability. The true RGO weight is bounded by1 under probability mu, so R is independently a probability measure.",
          "formula": "W(p+\\sqrt\\eta u)=Q(u)+C,\\quad r=(x\\mapsto(x-p)/\\sqrt\\eta)_\\#R=Z_Q^{-1}e^{-Q}du.",
          "lean": "actual_standardized_law; AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs; tilted_tilted; tilted_const; isProbabilityMeasure_tilted"
        },
        {
          "title": "Prove the pointwise gradient comparison",
          "text": "The actual C2 curvature theorem supplies eta-Lipschitz gradientrho. Its mode0 gives normgradrho(u)<=eta*normu; squaring keeps exactly eta^2. This is a real derivative estimate, not a gradient-output law certificate.",
          "formula": "\\|\\nabla\\rho(u)\\|^2\\le\\eta^2\\|u\\|^2.",
          "lean": "QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic; LipschitzWith.norm_sub_le"
        },
        {
          "title": "Integrate under the actual standardized posterior",
          "text": "Domination by the genuine position-square integrable function proves rho-gradient L2. Integral monotonicity and the genuine dimension bound give the last TWO comparisons of4.6 in squared form. No Talagrand/LSI/W2 estimate follows without its separate dependency.",
          "formula": "\\int\\|\\nabla\\rho\\|^2dr\\le\\eta^2\\int\\|u\\|^2dr\\le\\eta^2d.",
          "lean": "Integrable.mono'; integral_mono; integral_const_mul; memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Produce one measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. For literal rho(u)=V(p+sqrteta*u)-V(p)-sqrteta*inner(gradientV(p),u) and Q=normu^2/2+rho, produce C2, mode0, 0<=Hessrho<=etaI and I<=HessQ<=(1+eta)I. The actual RGO R=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)) is a probability measure, and its actual standardized pushforward r equals volume.tilted(-Q). Genuine position and rho-gradient L2 satisfy integral normu^2 dr<=d and integral normgradrho^2 dr<=eta^2 integral normu^2 dr<=eta^2 d. Only the last TWO comparisons of(4.6) are covered; the first W2 comparison is open.",
      "lean_proof": "Produce the true proximal point and base law; Differentiate the literal standardized potential; Derive actual curvature and the mode; Produce genuine Q normalization and the position moment; Identify the literal true RGO law; Prove the pointwise gradient comparison; Integrate under the actual standardized posterior",
      "astis_dependencies": [
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.FullRangeProximalGaussianOracle.full_range_proximal_gaussian_oracle",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.GibbsPositionMoment.gibbs_position_moment",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.StrongConvexGibbsIntegrability.integrable_exp_neg_of_strongConvexOn",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.HessianStrongConvexity.strongConvexOn_univ_of_fderiv2_lower",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs"
      ],
      "mathlib_dependencies": [
        "tilted_tilted",
        "tilted_const",
        "isProbabilityMeasure_tilted",
        "HasFDerivAt.comp",
        "HasFDerivAt.norm_sq",
        "inner_gradient_left",
        "integral_mono",
        "integral_const_mul",
        "memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm"
      ]
    }
  ]
